Changelog
[4.3] — 2026-04-01
Added
Protection plugin integration (ProtectionManager.java)
Chests no longer spawn inside protected territories. The plugin checks the spawn candidate location against any installed protection plugin before placing a chest. If the location is protected, a new random location is picked automatically. Integration works without any compile-time dependency — only softdepend in plugin.yml is required.
Supported plugins:

WorldGuard 7 — skips any location inside a named region (excluding __global__)
GriefPrevention — skips any location inside a player claim
GriefDefender 2 — skips any location inside a GD claim
Lands 5+ — skips any location inside a land area

Configuration (config.yml):
yamlprotection:
  enabled: true
  check-worldguard: true
  check-grief-prevention: true
  check-grief-defender: true
  check-lands: true
  max-protection-retries: 20   # extra retries on top of the base 15
Permission-based broadcast system
All player-facing announcements now respect individual permissions. This fixes the common issue on servers where all permissions are denied by default — previously only operators saw announcements.
PermissionControlsDefaultspawnchest.notify.spawnChest spawn message + titletruespawnchest.notify.coordinatesCoordinates shown in spawn messagetruespawnchest.notify.disappearChest disappear messagetruespawnchest.notify.countdownCountdown warningstruespawnchest.notify.bossbarBossBar visibilitytrue
Players without spawnchest.notify.coordinates still receive the spawn announcement — it just omits the coordinates ("A Legendary Chest has appeared somewhere in the world!").
New lang keys required in all language files:
yamlbroadcasts:
  chest-spawned-no-coords: "§6✦ §eA §6%tier% §ehas appeared somewhere in the world!"
  spawn-subtitle-hidden: "§eExplore the world to find it!"
system:
  chest-location-protected: "§7[SpawnChest] Location %x%, %z% is protected, retrying..."
BossBar (BossBarManager.java)
Optional BossBar showing the chest timer and active chest info. Disabled by default.
Configuration:
yamlfeatures:
  bossbar:
    enabled: false           # opt-in
    show-countdown: true     # time until next chest while idle
    show-active-chest: true  # tier + coordinates + expiry while a chest is alive
Behaviour:

While no chest is active: yellow bar counting down to next spawn
While a chest is active (unopened): green bar showing tier, coordinates, and time until despawn
Only shown to players with spawnchest.notify.bossbar permission
Automatically added/removed on join/quit

New public API methods on SpawnChestPlugin
javaplugin.getLastSpawnTime()        // long — epoch ms of last spawn
plugin.getSpawnInterval()        // long — configured interval in ms
plugin.getActiveChests()         // Map<String, ActiveChest>
plugin.getTierNamePublic(tier)   // String — localised tier name
Changed

Max spawn attempts increased from 15 to 15 + protection.max-protection-retries (default 35). Prevents the plugin giving up too early on heavily claimed servers.
plugin.yml permissions restructured: spawnchest.admin now uses children to inherit all sub-permissions (setchesttimer, resettimer, getlegendaryitems, testchestzone, giveapple) instead of duplicating default: op on each.
softdepend added to plugin.yml: WorldGuard, GriefPrevention, GriefDefender, Lands.
Plugin version bumped to 4.3 in plugin.yml.

Fixed

Broadcast methods no longer call Bukkit.broadcastMessage() for announcement types that have per-player permission gates. Each announcement iterates online players and checks the relevant spawnchest.notify.* node individually.


